{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development by reason of its failure to provide appropriate horizontal stacking and adequate internal floorspace for proposed Flat 3 would cumulatively result in sub-standard level of living accommodation for future occupiers of the proposed flats.&amp;nbsp; As such, the development is contrary to Policies D3 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), Policies DM 1 and DM 26 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and guidance in the Mayor of London Housing Supplementary Planning Guidance (2016) and adopted Residential Design Guide SPD(2010),&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development provides poorly located and restrictive internal corridor to transport refuse bins from their proposed garden storage location to the highway for presentation on collection days, resulting in substandard access arrangements. Furthermore, the proposed subdivision of the rear amenity space would visually break up the garden space and create unnecessary compact spaces which would break up the well spaced pattern of rear gardens, contrary to the high quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2023),&amp;nbsp; Policies D1 and D3 of the London Plan (2021), Policy DM 1 of the Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and Core Policy CS.1B of the Harrow Core Strategy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
